<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Scattered rains seen over Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Scattered rains seen over Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's meteorological department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Monday morning</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Canyon		    8.0</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	    17.5</p>
<p>    Kotmale		   6.5</p>
<p>    Laxapana		 17.0</p>
<p>    Moussakele		0</p>
<p>    Norton		    0</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    0</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   0</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  0</p>
<p>The department forecast scattered showers in the Central, Sabaragamuwa, Western and Souther provinces and over seas off southern and western coasts. Isolated thundershowers will prevail over the rest of the island during the afternoon and evening on Tuesday.</p>
</text>
